## Sync direction — settled 2026-08-10

Do not assume profield is always upstream. It is not:

- **Global layer: this repo is AHEAD.** `profield-frontend-pedagogy.md` is pass-5 (2026-08-10) with Ahmes dressing and §16. `profield/runs/.../pass1.edited.md` is pass-2/3 (2026-07-29) with **no Ahmes content**. *Do not overwrite this repo's map from `pass1.edited.md` — you would lose the dressing.*
- **Ibero + authorities: profield is upstream.** Both were absent here entirely and have been synced in. Re-sync by copying over and restoring the provenance banner.

## Retrieval vs. citation — the durable rule (2026-08-11)

Three layers, and **only one of them may be cited**:

| Layer | Role | May a guía cite it? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Ahmes vault** — `extraction.db` node + page | **Authoritative.** The claim is checkable against extracted text | ✅ **Yes — the only citable layer** |
| **DevIAC vectors** — `search_knowledge`, `project_slug=profield-frontend-pedagogy` | **Discovery.** Semantic retrieval across 16 ingested vaults; finds candidates fast | ❌ **Never cite a vector snippet.** Use it to locate, then open the node |
| **Athanor inject** | Field-grade collective search layer | ❌ infrastructure, not evidence |

**Discover in vectors, cite from nodes.** A snippet is a pointer, not a source: it has no stable page, it may be chunk-truncated mid-argument, and it cannot show you what the surrounding text qualifies. Every citation in the guías resolves to coat · node · page precisely so a reviewer can reopen it.

**A sibling rule, for technical facts rather than scholarly claims:** vendor/framework documentation (Astro docs, MDN, web.dev, W3C specs) is never a bibliography source, DOI/ISBN or not — it goes into the lesson as a labelled **platform note**, never as `(Author Year)`. This table above governs *how you find and cite research*; [`PLATFORM-NOTES-POLICY.mdc`](./PLATFORM-NOTES-POLICY.mdc) governs *how you use accurate technical facts without pretending they are research*. Written 2026-08-13 after an agent applied this repo's looser summary and had to be corrected against the stricter precedent already sitting in `temario/T3-....edited.md`'s Quarantine section.

**Cross-field harvest:** Cursor skill `provenance-layer` (`~/.cursor/skills/provenance-layer/`) — profile `frontend-pedagogy` in `profiles.md`. Same contract as CD: Athanor indexes · Ahmes cites.

> **Session caveat worth knowing:** MCP tool availability is **per session**, not global. An agent reporting that `search_knowledge` is unavailable is describing *its own registry*, not the DevIAC server's health. Diagnose at the level you can observe, and say which level you mean. If discovery is unavailable, the fallback — enumerate the manifest, query the DBs directly — is slower but **loses nothing citable**.

