## 🔴 The finding that prompted this sync

**The curriculum had outrun its own field map.**

The guías curriculares cite **18 Ahmes coats**, of which **8 are Ibero-American** (Batista, Correa, González-Videgaray, CEPAL, Digital Education Council, Gonçalves, Neves, RCS) — and the global map contained **zero** Ibero content. The venue ladder in [`../fe-research-line.mdc`](../fe-research-line.mdc) and the proposal in [`../fe-cohort-case-proposal.mdc`](../fe-cohort-case-proposal.mdc) were built from an authorities directory that **did not exist in this repository**.

Claims were traceable to vault nodes, so nothing was fabricated — but a reader of this repo alone could not reconstruct *why those sources*. That is now fixed.

**Rule going forward:** if a guía or lesson cites a layer, that layer must be present here. Curriculum may not cite grounding the repo does not carry.

